# launcHER.CNF - Ember quickboot template
#
# Keep this file beside the launcHER binary.
# The ELF itself may be renamed to anything (for example Soul Blade.ELF).
# When started without explicit target arguments, launcHER always looks for
# a file named launcHER.CNF in the directory it was launched from.
#
# Example OPL APPS layout:
#   +OPL/APPS/Soul Blade/Soul Blade.ELF
#   +OPL/APPS/Soul Blade/launcHER.CNF
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - Replace <GAME_FOLDER> with the bare folder name under EMBER/games.
#   - Do NOT add games/ or a .cue filename.
#   - arg= lines are global to every active path= line in this file.
#   - Leave only ONE profile below uncommented unless you intentionally want
#     fallback paths that share the exact same arguments.
#
# Example game argument:
#   arg=Final Fantasy VII
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHICH HDD DO I HAVE?
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# USB HDD / USB SSD:
#   path=mass?:/EMBER/ember.elf
#
# Internal HDD using exFAT:
#   path=ata:/EMBER/ember.elf
#
# APA-Jail / mixed APA+exFAT HDD, Ember on the exFAT side:
#   path=ata:/EMBER/ember.elf
#
# Internal APA/PFS HDD, or Ember inside a PFS partition:
#   path=hdd0:<PARTITION>:pfs:/EMBER/ember.elf
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   launcHER DOES NOT REQUIRE A DEDICATED __.EMBER PARTITION.
#   __.EMBER is only an example and can be convenient for organization
#   and free space. Use the PFS partition that actually contains EMBER.
#
# The question is not just "am I using an HDD?"
# The question is "where is EMBER stored on that HDD?"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE 1 - USB / removable / local devices
#
# USB HDDs and USB SSDs use the same mass-storage path as USB flash drives.
# These paths may share the same game argument, so multiple path= lines can
# be enabled together if you intentionally want launcHER to try them in order.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# path=mmce?:/EMBER/ember.elf
# path=mc?:/EMBER/ember.elf
# path=mass?:/EMBER/ember.elf
# path=usb?:/EMBER/ember.elf
# path=mx4sio:/EMBER/ember.elf
# path=ilink:/EMBER/ember.elf
# arg=<GAME_FOLDER>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE 2 - Internal exFAT HDD / APA-Jail exFAT side (ATA BDM)
#
# Use this when EMBER is stored on the exFAT filesystem of the internal HDD.
# This does NOT require a PFS partition.
# Keep the HDD powered for Ember after handoff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# path=ata:/EMBER/ember.elf
# arg=<GAME_FOLDER>
# arg=-dev9=NICHDD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE 3 - Internal APA/PFS HDD
#
# Use this only when EMBER itself is stored inside a PFS partition.
# Replace <PARTITION> with the PFS partition that actually contains EMBER.
#
# A dedicated __.EMBER partition is NOT required.
#
# Example using __.EMBER:
#   path=hdd0:__.EMBER:pfs:/EMBER/ember.elf
#
# Example using an existing __common partition:
#   path=hdd0:__common:pfs:/EMBER/ember.elf
#
# APA/PFS is special: launcHER uses the hdd0: path to locate/load Ember, but
# Ember itself must receive pfs0:/EMBER/ember.elf as argv[0] so its working
# directory resolves correctly. NICHDD also preserves the writable pfs0:
# mount through ExecPS2 for games, settings, and memory-card files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# path=hdd0:<PARTITION>:pfs:/EMBER/ember.elf
# arg=pfs0:/EMBER/ember.elf
# arg=<GAME_FOLDER>
# arg=-skip_argv0
# arg=-dev9=NICHDD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE 4 - UDPBD
# Keep the network adapter powered after handoff.
# IP configuration is read from mc?:/SYS-CONF/IPCONFIG.DAT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# path=udpbd:/EMBER/ember.elf
# arg=<GAME_FOLDER>
# arg=-dev9=NIC

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE 5 - UDPFS
# Keep the network adapter powered after handoff.
# IP configuration is read from mc?:/SYS-CONF/IPCONFIG.DAT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# path=udpfs:/EMBER/ember.elf
# arg=<GAME_FOLDER>
# arg=-dev9=NIC
